---
title: "Set change"
note: "Pyro's idea taken all the way: one continuous walk through places that have nothing to do with each other, and every clip changes the set in front of the camera by a visible action instead of a cut. Stagehands strike it, a giant hand swaps the diorama, the sky tears open, a train passes, the whole place is a painted flat that falls over (transitions/between, twenty of them, each with its own sound). Loop it on Motion Context with Run (Instant)."
tags: [loops, h3, reel, motion_context]
---
@h3 t2va 16:9
context: 22
style: live-action, cinematic, photorealistic, one continuous unbroken ten-second shot gliding forward at walking pace
MUSIC: N/A

CHUNK the first place
$place = {__world/landscapes__:2|__tour/rooms__}
SHOT 10s | tracking, slow
The camera glides forward at eye level through $place, taking it in. Light and air move through it, and nothing else happens yet.
SFX: $place.sfx
HANDOFF: the camera glides on through $place

CHUNK the set change repeat forever
$from = $place~1
$place = {__world/landscapes__:2|__tour/rooms__}
$to = $place
$shift = __transitions/between__
SHOT 10s | tracking, slow
The camera keeps gliding forward at the same steady pace. $shift. The camera glides on into $place as if nothing unusual had happened.
SFX: $shift.sfx; $place.sfx
HANDOFF: the camera glides on through $place
